    "created_at": "2018-08-16T15:45:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-16T15:45:47Z",
    "body": "I don't see a reason for border-image borders to behave differently from other type of borders.  But yes, we should specify somewhere how fieldset borders should be rendered in general.\r\nI have a attached a few more testcases on the bug you referenced above where Firefox renders it differently than Chrome. It appears that Chrome clips the border entirely in the block-axis whereas Firefox only clips it to the extent of the legend's border box (i.e. if the border is thicker than the legend's block-size then the border renders above/below it.)\r\nIt actually looks like both UAs handles its image borders and ordinary borders consistently.",
